{"status": "progress", "message": "Retrieved 138 candidate paragraphs; kept 3", "stage": "retrieve", "claim_index": 0, "data": {"kind": "retrieval", "pass": 1, "queries": ["Eiffel Tower", "Paris, France"], "candidates": 138, "by_source": {"web": 3, "wikipedia": 135}, "avgdl": 129.6, "top": [{"text": "Where is Eiffel Tower located on the world map? The Eiffel Tower is located in Paris, France. It stands in the heart of the city on the Champ de Mars, a large p", "source": "web", "dense": 0.89, "bm25": 21.14, "dense_rank": 1, "bm25_rank": 1, "rrf": 0.03279, "selected": true}, {"text": "The Eiffel Tower (/ \u02c8a\u026af\u0259l / \u24d8 EYE-f\u0259l; French: Tour Eiffel [tu\u0281 \u025bf\u025bl] \u24d8) is a lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engine", "source": "web", "dense": 0.784, "bm25": 12.47, "dense_rank": 2, "bm25_rank": 2, "rrf": 0.03226, "selected": true}, {"text": "The Eiffel Tower (  EYE-f\u0259l; French: Tour Eiffel [tu\u0281 \u025bf\u025bl] ) is a lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engineer Gustave E", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.775, "bm25": 11.79, "dense_rank": 4, "bm25_rank": 3, "rrf": 0.0315, "selected": true}, {"text": "Although initially criticised by some of France's leading artists and intellectuals for its design, it has since become a global cultural icon of France and one", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.723, "bm25": 7.62, "dense_rank": 5, "bm25_rank": 10, "rrf": 0.02967, "selected": false}, {"text": "During its construction, the Eiffel Tower surpassed the Washington Monument to become by far the tallest human-made structure in the world, a title it held for ", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.671, "bm25": 8.11, "dense_rank": 8, "bm25_rank": 8, "rrf": 0.02941, "selected": false}, {"text": "The stars of the European Union for the tower Eiffel Tower The Eiffel Tower (French: La Tour Eiffel, [tu\u0281 \u025bf\u025bl], IPA pronunciation: \"EYE-full\" English; \"Eiffel\"", "source": "web", "dense": 0.775, "bm25": 7.28, "dense_rank": 3, "bm25_rank": 15, "rrf": 0.02921, "selected": false}, {"text": "Excluding transmitters, the Eiffel Tower is the second tallest free-standing structure in France after the Millau Viaduct. The tower has three levels for visito", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.722, "bm25": 7.41, "dense_rank": 6, "bm25_rank": 13, "rrf": 0.02885, "selected": false}, {"text": "It was designated a monument historique in 1964, and was named part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site (\"Paris, Banks of the Seine\") in 1991. The tower is 330 metr", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.652, "bm25": 7.45, "dense_rank": 11, "bm25_rank": 11, "rrf": 0.02817, "selected": false}], "selected": 3, "echo_filtered": 0, "kept": 3}, "t": 5.912}
